description:
## Problem

Stagehand advertises screenshot baselines and diffs, but downstream games need a precise, stable workflow before agents can rely on it for visual regression tests.

## Task

Harden and document godot_screenshot_save_baseline and godot_screenshot_diff as generic primitives:
- baseline storage location and naming rules;
- refresh/update procedure;
- diff threshold semantics vs per-pixel sensitivity;
- selector-cropped screenshots;
- output artifacts for failed diffs;
- machine-readable result fields for agents.

## Acceptance

- A fixture test saves a baseline, changes the fixture state, and gets a failing diff with useful artifacts/result fields.
- Threshold and pixel_sensitivity semantics are documented with examples.
- No downstream game-specific assertions are added here.
